    "question_text": "In the following reaction sequence, the major product $\\mathbf{P}$ is formed.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/65VJZ6IJy8c-o86buKSkQTtePbf-UUSpW1Eyd2PytE8.original.fullsize.png\">\nGlycerol reacts completely with excess $\\mathbf{P}$ in the presence of an acid catalyst to form $\\mathbf{Q}$. Reaction of $\\mathbf{Q}$ with excess $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ followed by the treatment with $\\mathrm{CaCl}_2$ yields Ca-soap $\\mathbf{R}$, quantitatively. Starting with one mole of $\\mathbf{Q}$, the amount of $\\mathbf{R}$ produced in gram is ________.\n[Given, atomic weight: $\\mathrm{H}=1, \\mathrm{C}=12, \\mathrm{~N}=14, \\mathrm{O}=16, \\mathrm{Na}=23, \\mathrm{Cl}=35, \\mathrm{Ca}=40$ ]",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [],
    "correct_answer": 909,
    "solution_text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/FU-LArOFMNrHyc3DDcQnVLpDwqlq5F_MME0WmISMut0.original.fullsize.png\">\n$\\frac{3}{2}$ mole soap. $=\\frac{3}{2} \\times 606 \\mathrm{gm}=909 \\mathrm{gm}$",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Abnormal Behaviour of Formic Acid"
  },
  {
    "question_id": "64b16aa8f23ac7d519f9b66c",
    "type": "multipleCorrect",
    "difficulty_level": 3,
    "syllabus_category": "noChange",
    "question_structure": "default",
    "paper_year_title": "JEE Advanced 2023 (Paper 2)",
    "paper_year_short": "2023 (Paper 2)",
    "held_on": "2023-04-30T14:00:00.000Z",
    "question_text": "<p>In the following reactions, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> are the major products.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a269bb02-9884-4024-964d-22a1c1145cb0.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 110px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a9b909d7-d90e-47c2-bec5-44781080da22.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 80px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0d775c2e-aba1-490e-b8c1-74a5e393036c.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/d2b88317-9735-49a0-bd61-238cc9863345.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 107px;\" /></p><p>The correct statement(s) about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> is(are)</p>",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "cQVm8",
        "text": "P and Q are monomers of polymers dacron and glyptal, respectively.",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "BWvB7",
        "text": "P, Q, and R are dicarboxylic acids.",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "0mr2j",
        "text": "Compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math> are the same.",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "4UYZU",
        "text": "<strong>R</strong> does not undergo aldol condensation and <strong>S</strong> does not undergo Cannizzaro reaction.",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "4UYZU",
    "solution_text": "<p>Toluene part of the reactant in the first reaction&nbsp;undergoes oxidation with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, forms benzoic acid. In this conversion, alkyl part of toluene converts into carboxylic group. So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;is a monocarboxylic acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/9a0809ac-3caf-46c2-bd12-9e6d32fea27e.png\" style=\"width: 589px; height: 153px;\" /></p><p>Both ester and acid halides undergo hydrolysis to give carboxylic acid. Hence, the product&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is the dicarboxylic acid. And it is known as isophthalic acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7c15c884-db08-4875-bf1c-c5e3bc16be1a.png\" style=\"width: 530px; height: 156px;\" /></p><p>In the third reaction, ester undergo hydrolysis in the first step, which results beta keto acid. Beta keto acids are unstable. They liberate carbon dioxide on heating. The alpha methyl ketone formed undergo oxidation with chromic acid give carboxylic acid. Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is also isophthalic acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7832a67c-385f-42ec-9604-242ea1375764.png\" style=\"width: 618px; height: 514px;\" /></p><p>In the fourth reaction, the bromo part reacts with magnesium metal to give Grignard reagent. Grignard reagent give carboxylic acid upon reaction with carbon dioxide. Now during the hydrolysis of previous step acetal cleavage takes place and gives aldehyde functional group. This aldehyde converts to carboxylic acid with Tollen&#39;s reagent. This results the terephthalic acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c41496f5-e447-4c7a-849e-c96437945f0d.png\" style=\"width: 671px; height: 417px;\" /></p><p>The products&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>&nbsp;are dicarboxylic acids and does not undergo Aldol condensation reaction or Cannizzaro&#39;s reaction.</p>",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Preparation and Properties of Acid Derivatives"
  },
