    "held_on": "2023-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
    "question_text": "<p>Match the reactions (in the given stoichiometry of the reactants) in List-I with one of their products given in List-II and choose the correct option.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List-I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List-II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(P)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(1)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(Q)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(2)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(R)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(3)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(S)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(4)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>POCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>(5)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "S89Z3",
        "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "AlQrx",
        "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "Z9ghH",
        "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "sNRWE",
        "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "sNRWE",
    "solution_text": "<blockquote><p>Phosphorus trioxide reacts with water to form phosphorous acid,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>When acetic acid is heated with phosphorus pentachloride, acetyl chloride is obtained. In this reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math> group is converted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>COCl</mi></math> group. The side products are phosphorus oxychloride and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COCl</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>POCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;undergo disproportionation reaction with sodium hydroxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow/></mover><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>NaH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Due to the presence two&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;bonds,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;acts as reducing agent. It reduces&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Preparation and Properties of Acid Derivatives"
  },
