        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "8SnAy",
    "solution_text": "<blockquote><p>Styrene on hydroboration-oxidation reaction gives a primary alcohol. It follows anti-Markonikov&#39;s rule to give alcohol from alkenes. Primary alcohols give carboxylic acids on oxidation with Jone&#39;s reagent. The alpha chloro carboxylic acid is produced on HVZ reaction of carboxylic acid produced.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b84149e0-d266-4bf5-81a7-000aea26efce.png\" style=\"width: 697px; height: 167px;\" /></p><p>2-phenyl ethanol on reaction with thionyl chloride produces 1-chloro-2-phenylethane. The chloro group is replaced with cyano group. The cyanide on hydrolysis give carboxylic acid. The carboxylic acid undergoes acylation reaction in the presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>conc</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/4d71ea56-ee53-426f-8229-d207c2ab49b4.png\" style=\"width: 744px; height: 174px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Preparation and Properties of Carboxylic Acids"
  },
